    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-806" textLabel="gibberellin 2-oxidase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9AVA5" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="480.28173828125" centerY="1177.725341796875" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The &lt;i&gt;Oryza sativa GA2ox1&lt;/i&gt; gene was expressed in &lt;i&gt;E.coli&lt;/i&gt; and shown to encode for a gibberellin (GA) 2-oxidase (OsGA2ox1). Cell lysates of &lt;i&gt;E.coli&lt;/i&gt; expressing &lt;i&gt;GA2ox1&lt;/i&gt; could catalyze the 2-oxidation of a variety of GAs, including GA&lt;sub&gt;44&lt;/sub&gt;, GA&lt;sub&gt;20&lt;/sub&gt;, GA&lt;sub&gt;1&lt;/sub&gt;, GA&lt;sub&gt;9&lt;/sub&gt; and GA&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;; they were converted to GA&lt;sub&gt;98&lt;/sub&gt;, GA&lt;sub&gt;29&lt;/sub&gt;, GA&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;, GA&lt;sub&gt;51&lt;/sub&gt; and GA&lt;sub&gt;34&lt;/sub&gt;, respectively |CITS:[11244129]|. Moreover, transgenic rice plants ectopically expressing &lt;i&gt;GA2ox1&lt;/i&gt; were shown to have elevated levels of GA&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt; and GA&lt;sub&gt;29&lt;/sub&gt; |CITS:[11244129]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="MONOMER-806" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Phytozome" value="Os05t0158600-02" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pride" value="Q9AVA5" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Interpro" value="IPR026992" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pfam" value="PF14226" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Prosite" value="PS51471" />
